WEBVTT

00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:13.880
<i>I've fought demons several times 
since I left the city of the dead.</i>

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:19.040
<i>As someone trained by Blood and the others, 
and after fighting an undead god,</i>

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:22.510
<i>everyday demon riffraff 
are no match for me.</i>

00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:42.180
The Faraway Paladin

00:02:10.290 --> 00:02:12.490
<i>It's been quite a while since I departed,</i>

00:02:12.490 --> 00:02:14.450
<i>but I still haven't met any humans.</i>

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:17.200
<i>All I see is the occasional wild animal</i>

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:19.490
<i>and bizarre, distorted demons.</i>

00:02:22.010 --> 00:02:23.670
It's so cold...

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:27.050
<i>It's been 200 years since Blood 
and the others were alive.</i>

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:32.090
<i>Does that mean no humans have 
returned in 200 years?</i>

00:02:33.190 --> 00:02:36.210
<i>It's cold, but not cold enough for snow.</i>

00:03:13.910 --> 00:03:16.280
No people here, I guess...

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:24.190
A scar left by immense magic?

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:29.770
Gracefeel, Goddess of Light...

00:03:30.650 --> 00:03:34.960
Bring peace and guidance to the 
wandering souls in this land.

00:03:51.890 --> 00:03:53.790
Yeah, of course.

00:03:54.020 --> 00:03:56.260
It <i>has</i> been 200 years.

00:03:56.260 --> 00:03:58.010
The terrain's gonna change.

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:00.460
<i>Alarm</i>

00:04:00.460 --> 00:04:02.170
<i>Magic Ward</i>

00:04:02.170 --> 00:04:04.130
<i>Insect Ward</i>

00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:11.680
<i>I'm running out of preserved food.</i>

00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:14.400
<i>I can get bread by praying 
for the blessing,</i>

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:18.080
<i>and I can purify water, 
so I'll hold out for a while...</i>

00:04:20.850 --> 00:04:23.690
<i>but I hope I reach someplace 
populated soon.</i>

00:04:32.570 --> 00:04:35.670
If I keep walking downriver, 
I should eventually...

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:44.890
A demon? No!

00:04:45.170 --> 00:04:46.550
It's a huge boar!

00:04:55.480 --> 00:04:56.570
I should finish it...

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:00.240
What's this?

00:05:03.940 --> 00:05:05.580
<i>The same white fletching...</i>

00:05:06.100 --> 00:05:07.370
<i>A hunter?</i>

00:05:07.730 --> 00:05:09.480
<i>This is not an ideal scenario.</i>

00:05:09.950 --> 00:05:12.490
<i>We both found our weapons 
in a place like this.</i>

00:05:12.920 --> 00:05:14.620
<i>Depending on what he does...</i>

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:17.280
<i>I finally met another person.</i>

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:19.110
<i>I should show him I'm not a threat.</i>

00:05:19.510 --> 00:05:21.280
<i>Should I drop my weapon?</i>

00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:23.380
<i>He might attack, though.</i>

00:05:23.380 --> 00:05:26.530
<i>Pray for the blessing and show 
what a devout follower I am?</i>

00:05:26.950 --> 00:05:29.470
<i>That might be mistaken for an attack.</i>

00:05:30.110 --> 00:05:32.300
<i>I need to choose my words carefully.</i>

00:05:32.710 --> 00:05:35.640
<i>I'm an outsider with no way 
to prove my identity.</i>

00:05:39.560 --> 00:05:42.730
When we meet, the stars gleam.

00:05:43.860 --> 00:05:45.090
<i>Ancient Elvish?</i>

00:05:45.550 --> 00:05:47.880
Are you related to the elves?

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:48.830
No.

00:05:48.830 --> 00:05:52.080
But I could see that 
you're related to them.

00:05:52.470 --> 00:05:54.860
Your bow is elven, is it not?

00:05:57.320 --> 00:05:59.950
Heh. Well, you're not wrong.

00:06:02.170 --> 00:06:07.630
Episode 6 
Archer of Beast Woods

00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:06.360
Well, whatever.

00:06:06.360 --> 00:06:09.340
Anyway, did you finish off that boar?

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:11.790
Oh... Yes, it was me.

00:06:11.790 --> 00:06:13.630
That was my quarry.

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:15.890
You took the kill from me.

00:06:15.890 --> 00:06:16.630
S—

00:06:17.340 --> 00:06:21.000
<i>I almost said "sorry" out of 
habit from my previous life.</i>

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:25.260
You're right. It charged 
at me out of nowhere,

00:06:25.260 --> 00:06:27.190
so I had no choice but to protect myself.

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:28.450
Still...

00:06:28.760 --> 00:06:30.690
<i>This will take some negotiation.</i>

00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:33.400
Since I'm the one who killed it,

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:35.910
I believe I, at least, 
have that much right to it.

00:06:39.220 --> 00:06:41.970
Well, you do have a point.

00:06:42.790 --> 00:06:44.930
Oh, damn it. It's broken.

00:06:44.930 --> 00:06:46.770
And I don't have many left...

00:06:46.770 --> 00:06:49.030
<i>Is metal hard to come by?</i>

00:06:50.080 --> 00:06:52.590
<i>We negotiated a few other 
things after that.</i>

00:06:52.830 --> 00:06:55.460
<i>The silver-haired half-elf 
was a skilled negotiator,</i>

00:06:55.460 --> 00:06:58.100
<i>so I was sort of at his 
mercy for the most part,</i>

00:06:58.440 --> 00:07:00.280
<i>but he agreed to give 
me the boar's shoulder</i>

00:07:00.280 --> 00:07:03.100
<i>in exchange for helping him butcher it.</i>

00:07:03.330 --> 00:07:05.230
Wow, you know your stuff, huh?

00:07:08.940 --> 00:07:11.440
<i>I'm sorry. You have my gratitude.</i>

00:07:11.440 --> 00:07:13.040
<i>We'll make good use of you.</i>

00:07:13.440 --> 00:07:15.420
You're pretty devoted.

00:07:15.770 --> 00:07:16.950
Anyway...

00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:20.630
The front leg is yours.

00:07:20.630 --> 00:07:22.550
And that takes care of the portioning.

00:07:22.550 --> 00:07:23.480
Yeah.

00:07:24.940 --> 00:07:27.030
I guess we should eat the liver, at least.

00:07:27.030 --> 00:07:28.300
It'll go bad fast.

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:30.600
Oh, I've got a pan we can use.

00:07:34.940 --> 00:07:36.460
Flammo Ignis.

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:36.310
Burn, Flames

00:07:37.260 --> 00:07:39.430
Hey, you're pretty good with your hands.

00:07:39.700 --> 00:07:41.040
Yeah, sorta.

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:43.880
<i>I should keep my magic a secret for now.</i>

00:07:45.130 --> 00:07:47.040
So, now we just wait.

00:07:47.040 --> 00:07:47.910
Yeah.

00:07:49.100 --> 00:07:50.410
Earth-Mother Mater,

00:07:50.710 --> 00:07:52.500
and all the virtuous gods,

00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:56.290
we give thanks for your grace 
as we partake in this meal.

00:07:56.290 --> 00:07:59.230
Please bless the food before us,

00:07:59.230 --> 00:08:02.670
that it may nourish our 
bodies and our souls.

00:08:02.670 --> 00:08:04.760
You really are devoted, huh?

00:08:05.010 --> 00:08:07.870
<i>He doesn't seem to be much of a believer.</i>

00:08:08.190 --> 00:08:09.590
Okay, let's eat.

00:08:08.370 --> 00:08:12.050
<i>But I'm the one with memories of my past 
life, while he seems closer to nature.</i>

00:08:09.980 --> 00:08:11.630
We give thanks for this bounty.

00:08:11.630 --> 00:08:12.460
Let's eat.

00:08:17.170 --> 00:08:18.160
Hot!

00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:19.030
Good stuff!

00:08:19.570 --> 00:08:21.520
<i>Ah, this is the best!</i>

00:08:24.740 --> 00:08:25.450
Huh?

00:08:25.840 --> 00:08:27.550
You want directions?

00:08:27.550 --> 00:08:30.500
Well, I mean... 
It's kind of hard to explain...

00:08:30.500 --> 00:08:31.930
I'm not sure how to put it...

00:08:31.930 --> 00:08:33.440
You don't look familiar, either.

00:08:33.710 --> 00:08:35.690
Seriously, where <i>are</i> you from?

00:08:36.140 --> 00:08:40.650
<i>Telling him I was raised in the ruins by 
three undead probably wouldn't help.</i>

00:08:41.340 --> 00:08:43.250
I came from the south.

00:08:43.250 --> 00:08:46.400
The south? Bro, there's nothing 
further south than this.

00:08:46.400 --> 00:08:47.090
Huh?

00:08:47.090 --> 00:08:49.480
This is as far south as 
mankind has ever gone,

00:08:49.480 --> 00:08:51.530
Beast Woods in Southmark.

00:08:52.330 --> 00:08:54.540
I did come from the south, though.

00:08:54.740 --> 00:08:56.050
It's a long story.

00:08:56.470 --> 00:09:00.770
Oh, are you an adventurer who 
scrounges for treasures in ruins?

00:09:00.770 --> 00:09:02.820
Yeah, something like that.

00:09:02.820 --> 00:09:04.560
And you got lost?

00:09:04.880 --> 00:09:05.850
Yeah.

00:09:05.850 --> 00:09:09.120
I've never seen an adventurer 
as absent-minded as you.

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:10.530
Well, whatever.

00:09:10.900 --> 00:09:12.920
Just keep following the river downstream,

00:09:12.920 --> 00:09:15.690
and you'll reach a small 
town in a couple of days.

00:09:15.930 --> 00:09:17.520
You can figure the rest out from there.

00:09:17.520 --> 00:09:18.810
Thanks.

00:09:18.810 --> 00:09:20.420
Yeah, well, good luck.

00:09:20.420 --> 00:09:24.610
Hey, if it's on the way, can we stop 
by the settlement you're living in?

00:09:29.080 --> 00:09:29.890
Um...

00:09:29.890 --> 00:09:30.760
No.

00:09:30.760 --> 00:09:33.110
I don't wanna get involved 
with you for even a second.

00:09:33.110 --> 00:09:34.130
Get a clue.

00:09:35.130 --> 00:09:36.820
<i>Yeah, of course not.</i>

00:09:36.820 --> 00:09:39.700
<i>Who'd want a total stranger in armor 
like this following them home?</i>

00:09:40.120 --> 00:09:41.380
Sorry.

00:09:41.640 --> 00:09:43.170
So don't follow me.

00:09:43.170 --> 00:09:45.610
W-Will you be okay with no light?

00:09:45.610 --> 00:09:48.380
That's nothing you need to worry about.

00:09:53.890 --> 00:09:55.340
Are those...

00:09:55.340 --> 00:09:56.390
Fairies.

00:09:57.030 --> 00:09:58.650
I've never seen them before.

00:09:58.970 --> 00:10:01.410
<i>They say elves, as followers 
of the goddess of fae,</i>

00:10:01.410 --> 00:10:04.830
<i>have a strong affinity 
with other fae minions.</i>

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:06.940
<i>I guess that goes for him, too.</i>

00:10:06.940 --> 00:10:07.840
Later.

00:10:07.840 --> 00:10:09.160
Uh... I'm Will.

00:10:09.450 --> 00:10:11.250
William G. Maryblood.

00:10:11.250 --> 00:10:12.160
What's your name?

00:10:13.600 --> 00:10:16.190
Menel. Meneldor.

00:10:16.920 --> 00:10:19.170
Not that we'll ever see each other again.

00:10:19.430 --> 00:10:21.270
Try not to die on the road.

00:10:25.330 --> 00:10:26.650
<i>Meneldor...</i>

00:10:27.030 --> 00:10:31.190
<i>In Elvish, I think that means 
"a very fast-flying eagle."</i>

00:10:31.580 --> 00:10:35.580
<i>He was a bit crude, but it 
was fun talking to him.</i>

00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:40.160
<i>He looked around my age, but they 
say half-elves are long-lived,</i>

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:42.840
<i>so he might be a lot older than me.</i>

00:10:44.890 --> 00:10:48.290
Oh, right... I should be close to a town.

00:10:51.140 --> 00:10:54.530
If I'll be getting more soon, 
I might as well indulge tonight.

00:10:58.950 --> 00:11:01.770
<i>I'll start by heading 
downriver to the town,</i>

00:11:01.770 --> 00:11:04.850
<i>and I'll try to get some information there.</i>

00:11:10.540 --> 00:11:13.990
O light, my light...

00:11:14.410 --> 00:11:17.740
As you travel, I pray:

00:11:18.340 --> 00:11:21.820
bring light to the faraway darkness.

00:11:29.840 --> 00:11:30.990
Menel!

00:11:32.240 --> 00:11:35.390
Was that... a divine revelation?

00:11:35.800 --> 00:11:36.850
Lumen!

00:11:36.050 --> 00:11:36.710
Light

00:11:38.850 --> 00:11:41.090
<i>A tragedy is about to befall a nearby village,</i>

00:11:41.470 --> 00:11:44.000
<i>and Menel is going to be caught up in it!</i>

00:11:46.470 --> 00:11:48.100
Inveniret Humanum!

00:11:46.600 --> 00:11:47.930
Find Human

00:11:48.920 --> 00:11:49.840
That way!

00:11:53.260 --> 00:11:54.340
There it is!

00:11:58.300 --> 00:11:59.910
Did I make it in time?

00:11:59.910 --> 00:12:01.110
Erasus!

00:11:59.990 --> 00:12:00.860
Erasure

00:12:08.920 --> 00:12:12.230
I thought I saw something 
shining in the forest.

00:12:12.230 --> 00:12:13.990
Sure you weren't just seeing things?

00:12:15.540 --> 00:12:18.570
<i>Thank goodness. If I tell 
them I know Menel—</i>

00:12:19.550 --> 00:12:20.420
Wha—

00:12:20.420 --> 00:12:22.150
Hide! Get behind me!

00:12:22.150 --> 00:12:22.590
Huh?!

00:12:22.590 --> 00:12:23.490
Hurry!

00:12:26.720 --> 00:12:28.230
<i>Raiders?!</i>

00:12:28.960 --> 00:12:30.890
<i>Menel's village is going to be attacked?</i>

00:12:30.890 --> 00:12:32.840
<i>Menel's going to caught up in a disaster?</i>

00:12:33.060 --> 00:12:36.160
<i>No... How a divine revelation is 
interpreted is up to the interpreter!</i>

00:12:38.090 --> 00:12:40.180
<i>It can't be...</i>

00:12:41.230 --> 00:12:44.190
<i>How could I have been such a fool?</i>

00:12:44.740 --> 00:12:47.190
<i>Meneldor isn't the victim of this tragedy.</i>

00:12:48.050 --> 00:12:49.620
<i>He's the perpetrator.</i>

00:12:51.780 --> 00:12:53.840
Go. Secure the village.

00:12:53.840 --> 00:12:55.160
I'll deal with this one.

00:12:56.210 --> 00:12:57.910
Menel! Why?!

00:12:57.910 --> 00:13:00.580
I told you not to follow me.

00:13:01.250 --> 00:13:02.430
Die.

00:13:05.310 --> 00:13:07.890
Everyone! Wake up! Wake up!

00:13:06.770 --> 00:13:08.320
We're under attack!

00:13:08.320 --> 00:13:09.640
Get your weapons!

00:13:11.010 --> 00:13:12.380
Acceleratio!

00:13:11.180 --> 00:13:12.220
Accelerate

00:13:15.630 --> 00:13:17.920
Gnomes, O gnomes, slip underfoot!

00:13:20.110 --> 00:13:23.930
<i>I have no strategy against 
someone who can use fairies.</i>

00:13:23.930 --> 00:13:24.910
<i>In that case...</i>

00:13:27.400 --> 00:13:28.350
Huh?!

00:13:28.350 --> 00:13:29.910
<i>He doesn't even realize</i>

00:13:29.910 --> 00:13:32.740
<i>that if your muscles are built up enough,</i>

00:13:32.740 --> 00:13:35.120
<i>you can solve most any problem by force!</i>

00:13:35.120 --> 00:13:36.220
Damn it!

00:13:36.220 --> 00:13:38.110
Salamander, burn him alive!

00:13:42.970 --> 00:13:43.790
Seriously?!

00:13:47.500 --> 00:13:50.210
You're really damn strong.

00:13:58.550 --> 00:14:03.190
<i>I need to subdue them all before 
anyone gets hurt or killed.</i>

00:14:03.440 --> 00:14:05.530
Spiderweb, Bind

00:14:03.460 --> 00:14:05.570
Araneum, Obligatio.

00:14:05.820 --> 00:14:07.420
I'm telling you...

00:14:06.350 --> 00:14:07.670
We oughta string them up!

00:14:06.910 --> 00:14:09.320
First off... Hey! I said <i>first off</i>...

00:14:07.670 --> 00:14:08.930
Listen to me!

00:14:09.320 --> 00:14:11.130
They attacked us outta nowhere!

00:14:11.130 --> 00:14:13.380
Look, in the first place...

00:14:13.380 --> 00:14:16.650
Hate to let a warrior priest 
see us actin' like this.

00:14:16.650 --> 00:14:19.340
Thank you again for your help earlier.

00:14:19.340 --> 00:14:21.060
My name's John.

00:14:21.060 --> 00:14:22.840
My name is William.

00:14:23.270 --> 00:14:27.610
Folks from many places, all with different 
ideas about law, drift to this village naturally.

00:14:27.610 --> 00:14:29.420
It's always like this.

00:14:30.120 --> 00:14:33.840
<i>This village is in an area of 
Southmark known as Beast Woods,</i>

00:14:33.840 --> 00:14:36.620
<i>and it apparently falls under the 
rule of the Fertile Kingdom.</i>

00:14:36.980 --> 00:14:41.560
<i>But the law and authority of the kingdom 
doesn't reach these dangerous remote regions,</i>

00:14:41.880 --> 00:14:47.170
<i>so the area is dotted with villages populated 
by criminals, fugitives with no relatives,</i>

00:14:47.170 --> 00:14:50.240
<i>adventures who scavenge the 
ruins, and other outsiders.</i>

00:14:50.780 --> 00:14:53.540
Of course, I'm one of them myself.

00:14:55.880 --> 00:14:58.290
What's going to happen to them?

00:14:58.290 --> 00:15:01.520
I don't know, either.

00:15:02.170 --> 00:15:06.850
They're from a neighboring village 
about a day's travel from here.

00:15:06.850 --> 00:15:08.140
A neighboring village?

00:15:08.140 --> 00:15:10.590
Neither of our villages 
are all that well-off,

00:15:10.590 --> 00:15:13.420
but I thought they, at least, 
had enough stored up for the winter.

00:15:13.780 --> 00:15:16.340
And we've always gotten 
along well enough...

00:15:16.700 --> 00:15:22.360
Also, that silver-haired half-elf is a 
well-known wandering hunter in these parts.

00:15:22.360 --> 00:15:25.600
He's helped us get rid of dangerous 
beasts lots of times, but now...

00:15:26.960 --> 00:15:28.360
Now, now.

00:15:28.700 --> 00:15:31.260
I'm sure everyone's worn out 
from all this talking.

00:15:31.710 --> 00:15:34.000
Take a break and have some water.

00:15:34.340 --> 00:15:36.300
This is Tom, our chief elder.

00:15:36.680 --> 00:15:40.950
Warrior priest, John has told me about you.

00:15:41.260 --> 00:15:44.950
Allow this old man to offer 
his gratitude, as well.

00:15:44.950 --> 00:15:49.310
Oh, no. This is all thanks to the 
guidance of the goddess of light.

00:15:49.310 --> 00:15:50.580
Ah...

00:15:50.580 --> 00:15:55.100
In that case, I must thank 
this goddess, as well.

00:15:55.920 --> 00:15:58.660
Now, warrior priest...

00:15:59.800 --> 00:16:05.890
Can I assume that if anything were to 
happen here, you would protect us?

00:16:08.330 --> 00:16:09.350
Yes.

00:16:09.350 --> 00:16:13.430
I swear on Gracefeel's light that 
I will protect everyone here.

00:16:14.090 --> 00:16:18.990
Then we don't need to worry about our 
safety if those ruffians attack again.

00:16:19.350 --> 00:16:24.080
Everyone, I believe we should wake 
them and ask why they've done this.

00:16:24.080 --> 00:16:25.210
Do you agree?

00:16:25.210 --> 00:16:26.780
We should hang them!

00:16:26.780 --> 00:16:28.490
That'll be hard to do if you get attached.

00:16:28.490 --> 00:16:30.640
Guys like them oughta be ended quick!

00:16:30.910 --> 00:16:34.130
But it's dangerous to do that 
before we know anything.

00:16:34.130 --> 00:16:37.020
The warrior priest will help us.

00:16:37.440 --> 00:16:41.350
<i>It seems like he wants to question 
them before proceeding.</i>

00:16:42.760 --> 00:16:45.860
Demons. Our village was 
destroyed by demons.

00:16:45.860 --> 00:16:49.330
Many died. Half of our village.

00:16:49.330 --> 00:16:51.970
With our women, children, and wounded,

00:16:51.970 --> 00:16:55.870
we were left with no food or 
shelter in the cold of winter.

00:16:55.870 --> 00:17:00.110
If we're doomed to die with only the shirts 
on our backs, then we might as well...

00:17:01.050 --> 00:17:03.250
I'm the one who suggested the raid.

00:17:03.830 --> 00:17:05.980
We wouldn't stand a chance 
fighting the demons.

00:17:06.590 --> 00:17:11.500
I said we'd be better off looting a village and 
going somewhere, anywhere, than just dying.

00:17:12.390 --> 00:17:15.960
An old lady in that village, 
Marple, helped me out a lot.

00:17:16.410 --> 00:17:19.120
What became of Marple?

00:17:19.840 --> 00:17:21.080
She died.

00:17:22.590 --> 00:17:23.710
I see.

00:17:23.960 --> 00:17:27.110
Just hang me. It was my idea.

00:17:27.110 --> 00:17:29.340
I deceived these guys, that's all.

00:17:29.340 --> 00:17:30.680
Let them go.

00:17:32.270 --> 00:17:33.080
Please.

00:17:33.430 --> 00:17:34.780
No way we can do that!

00:17:34.780 --> 00:17:35.580
Like hell!

00:17:35.580 --> 00:17:36.910
Hang 'em all!

00:17:37.700 --> 00:17:40.070
We owe a debt to this hunter.

00:17:40.430 --> 00:17:43.710
And I sympathize with the 
people of your village.

00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:46.090
However...

00:17:46.960 --> 00:17:49.110
We have no choice but to hang you.

00:17:52.870 --> 00:17:54.480
<i>Since they have nowhere to go,</i>

00:17:54.480 --> 00:17:57.100
<i>if they're set free, 
they'll just loot again.</i>

00:17:57.820 --> 00:18:01.060
<i>They have to be killed, 
for the safety of the village.</i>

00:18:01.060 --> 00:18:02.690
<i>That's the smart choice.</i>

00:18:03.600 --> 00:18:06.770
<i>But my mother told me,</i>

00:18:07.540 --> 00:18:11.430
<i>"Love others without fear of 
loss, and do good things."</i>

00:18:12.060 --> 00:18:13.520
<i>And my father told me,</i>

00:18:13.870 --> 00:18:16.040
<i>"Move forward with faith 
in the results you'll achieve,"</i>

00:18:16.040 --> 00:18:18.340
<i>and "Don't get so stressed 
that you freeze in place."</i>

00:18:19.060 --> 00:18:23.020
<i>I still carry their words 
with me, right here.</i>

00:18:23.510 --> 00:18:24.250
Excuse me!

00:18:26.590 --> 00:18:30.100
<i>I will overturn this hopeless 
situation before me.</i>

00:18:30.950 --> 00:18:32.950
Can this be resolved with money?

00:18:34.160 --> 00:18:36.710
Compensation, monetary atonement...

00:18:36.710 --> 00:18:38.590
Do you have that custom here?

00:18:38.590 --> 00:18:40.400
Well, yeah, we do...

00:18:40.400 --> 00:18:42.570
But who's gonna pay that?

00:18:42.570 --> 00:18:43.800
These guys are flat broke.

00:18:43.800 --> 00:18:45.810
I'll pay the money.

00:18:50.180 --> 00:18:53.640
Why do this, warrior priest?

00:18:53.830 --> 00:18:57.060
Because demons are my archenemies.

00:18:57.060 --> 00:18:59.230
They killed my parents.

00:18:59.520 --> 00:19:02.660
Plus, I swore to the goddess 
of light that I would

00:19:02.660 --> 00:19:05.630
banish evil and save the suffering.

00:19:05.960 --> 00:19:09.760
We should assist those who have 
suffered at the hands of demons.

00:19:10.460 --> 00:19:13.960
We can't allow a village 
occupied by demons to exist.

00:19:13.960 --> 00:19:15.360
I'll go and fight them.

00:19:15.830 --> 00:19:19.490
And I would like to hire that 
young man there to accompany me.

00:19:22.000 --> 00:19:25.460
He is an excellent hunter who 
knows this forest, right?

00:19:25.460 --> 00:19:29.180
I will need his talents to 
help me pursue the demons.

00:19:29.180 --> 00:19:31.010
Of course, I will pay handsomely.

00:19:31.340 --> 00:19:33.700
Are you sure about this?

00:19:33.700 --> 00:19:36.380
I feel like we're the only ones 
benefiting from this deal...

00:19:36.380 --> 00:19:40.770
It must be a reward for your 
exemplary day-to-day conduct.

00:19:41.230 --> 00:19:45.730
Gracefeel, the goddess of light who governs 
souls and the cycle of death and rebirth,

00:19:46.130 --> 00:19:50.800
is always looking upon your daily 
lives with compassionate eyes.

00:19:53.560 --> 00:19:54.600
Wow...

00:19:54.600 --> 00:19:56.170
What is this?

00:19:59.270 --> 00:20:01.220
Untie them.

00:20:01.220 --> 00:20:02.310
Right!

00:20:03.260 --> 00:20:06.790
I managed to overcome that... I think?

00:20:08.230 --> 00:20:12.170
<i>I had a feeling that, somewhere, 
some god was giving me a tiny smile.</i>

00:20:15.900 --> 00:20:17.990
<i>The people of the village that was attacked</i>

00:20:17.990 --> 00:20:20.750
<i>took in all of the villagers who 
weren't involved in the raid.</i>

00:20:21.330 --> 00:20:24.790
<i>Part of it was to use them as hostages, 
I'm sure, but safe is safe.</i>

00:20:26.520 --> 00:20:28.990
What are you after?

00:20:29.710 --> 00:20:32.770
I'm not hiding anything. 
I meant what I said.

00:20:32.770 --> 00:20:34.600
Because you're a warrior priest?

00:20:35.050 --> 00:20:36.050
Well...

00:20:36.350 --> 00:20:39.290
Oh, I almost forgot. 
I know it's already after the fact,

00:20:39.290 --> 00:20:43.340
but you will let me hire you to take back 
the village and destroy the demons, right?

00:20:43.540 --> 00:20:47.370
I'm the guy who instigated 
a raid and murder.

00:20:47.370 --> 00:20:49.020
You don't think I should be punished?

00:20:49.020 --> 00:20:51.720
I already cleared your debt 
by paying reparations.

00:20:52.110 --> 00:20:56.010
Besides, it was the only way you could 
help those starving people, right?

00:20:56.010 --> 00:20:58.280
You don't think I might betray you?

00:20:58.500 --> 00:21:01.780
If you do, it's the people of the 
neighboring village who'll suffer.

00:21:02.740 --> 00:21:04.180
You're too damn nice.

00:21:04.960 --> 00:21:07.800
One of these days, you'll be 
picked apart and left for dead.

00:21:07.800 --> 00:21:10.230
W-Well, I'll be careful.

00:21:10.500 --> 00:21:13.350
Okay, sure. I'll work for you.

00:21:13.350 --> 00:21:15.340
I do need money, after all.

00:21:15.650 --> 00:21:16.680
Thanks.

00:21:25.410 --> 00:21:27.460
So what are you gonna 
do for the time being,

00:21:27.460 --> 00:21:29.160
boss?

00:21:29.420 --> 00:21:32.610
The demons have occupied the 
neighboring village, right?

00:21:35.260 --> 00:21:38.240
I guess we'll just charge in. 
We don't have much time.

00:21:38.240 --> 00:21:40.010
Whoa, are you insane?

00:21:40.010 --> 00:21:42.540
There are a lot of them, 
and they've got demon beasts.

00:21:42.540 --> 00:21:44.190
You got a plan? What are our odds?

00:21:44.190 --> 00:21:45.850
It'll be fine. I'm used to them.

00:21:48.200 --> 00:21:51.290
Well, you're right that we gotta hurry.

00:21:51.960 --> 00:21:54.810
The people who died might've 
turned undead by now.

00:21:55.660 --> 00:21:59.780
<i>If that's true, I need to 
return them to the cycle</i>

00:22:00.230 --> 00:22:02.170
<i>before they get lost and end up stuck here.</i>

00:23:35.510 --> 00:23:39.970
Episode 7
Traumatic Memory
